§ `Regulation 16: the inherited amount`

-- (1): the spouse died before 6 April 2016; the person was under pensionable age; not married again.
#ASSERT `regulation 16(1): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020`
#ASSERT `regulation 16(1): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 5 Apr 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020`
-- 6 April 2016 is not "before 6th April 2016".
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 16(1): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 6 Apr 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 16(1): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person married again before pensionable age`)
-- Over pensionable age when the spouse died: not (1).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 16(1): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Mar 2015, person over pensionable age (reached 1 Jan 2015)`)
-- Exactly on the day the person reaches pensionable age: neither under nor over (fork F20). Asserted.
#ASSERT `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` `spouse died on the day the person reaches pensionable age` EQUALS `exactly at pensionable age, which is neither under nor over it`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 16(1): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died on the day the person reaches pensionable age`)
#ASSERT `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `under pensionable age`
#ASSERT `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` `spouse died 1 Mar 2015, person over pensionable age (reached 1 Jan 2015)` EQUALS `over pensionable age`

-- (2): the spouse reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 but died on or after it; the person under pensionable age.
#ASSERT `regulation 16(2): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2010, GRB 10 a week`
#ASSERT `regulation 16(2): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 6 Apr 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2010, GRB 10 a week`
-- A spouse who reached pensionable age on 6 April 2016 did not reach it "before" that day.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 16(2): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age on 6 Apr 2016, GRB 10 a week`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 16(2): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 5 Apr 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2010, GRB 10 a week`)

-- (3): same spouse facts, but the person was over pensionable age when the spouse died.
#ASSERT `regulation 16(3): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reached pensionable age 1 May 2016` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2010, GRB 10 a week`
-- Whether the person married again does not matter in (3).
#ASSERT `regulation 16(3): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person over pensionable age and married again (irrelevant)` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2010, GRB 10 a week`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 16(3): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2010, GRB 10 a week`)

-- Which paragraph applies.
#ASSERT `regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` EQUALS JUST `regulation 16(1) applies`
#ASSERT `regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2010, GRB 10 a week` EQUALS JUST `regulation 16(2) applies`
#ASSERT `regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reached pensionable age 1 May 2016` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2010, GRB 10 a week` EQUALS JUST `regulation 16(3) applies`
-- None: a spouse who died after 6 April 2016 having reached pensionable age after it. Outside regulation 16.
#ASSERT `regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age on 6 Apr 2016, GRB 10 a week` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` `spouse died on the day the person reaches pensionable age` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (6): the date on which the GRB rate is determined.
#ASSERT `regulation 16(6): the date as at which the deceased's graduated retirement benefit rate is determined` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `regulation 16(1) applies` EQUALS YMD 2020 1 1
#ASSERT `regulation 16(6): the date as at which the deceased's graduated retirement benefit rate is determined` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `regulation 16(2) applies` EQUALS YMD 2020 1 1
#ASSERT `regulation 16(6): the date as at which the deceased's graduated retirement benefit rate is determined` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reached pensionable age 1 May 2016` `regulation 16(3) applies` EQUALS YMD 2016 6 1

-- (4): half of the weekly rate.
#ASSERT `regulation 16(4): the inherited amount, in pounds per week` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `regulation 16(4): the inherited amount, in pounds per week` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10.50 a week` EQUALS 5.25

§ `Regulation 15: the survivor's state pension`

#ASSERT `regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` `married on 1 Jun 1990`
-- (a): has reached pensionable age by the day asked (the day itself counts).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `person has not yet reached pensionable age on the day` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` `married on 1 Jun 1990`)
#ASSERT `regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `person reaches pensionable age on the day asked` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` `married on 1 Jun 1990`
-- (b): the spouse died while they were married; and regulation 1(5).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `the spouse had not died while married` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` `married on 1 Jun 1990`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `married, but one was married to a third person` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` `married on 1 Jun 1990`)
-- Regulation 1(5) is about marriage only: a civil partnership stands (fork F9). Asserted.
#ASSERT `regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `civil partners, one in a marriage to a third person (regulation 1(5) is silent)` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` `married on 1 Jun 1990`
-- (c): the marriage or civil partnership before 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT `regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` `married on 5 Apr 2016`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` `married on 6 Apr 2016`)
-- (d): an inherited amount under regulation 16 is needed.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age on 6 Apr 2016, GRB 10 a week` `married on 1 Jun 1990`)

-- (3): the weekly rate is the inherited amount; none where there is no inherited amount.
#ASSERT `regulation 15(3): the weekly rate of the state pension under regulation 15` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age 1 Jan 2005, GRB 10 a week` EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `regulation 15(3): the weekly rate of the state pension under regulation 15` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `spouse reached pensionable age on 6 Apr 2016, GRB 10 a week` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 17: up-rating`

-- Full rate 100 before the increase; percentages: 10% for the full rate, 5% for an order.
-- S at least F: paragraphs (8) and (9): the order's percentage of R.
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 10 100 100 NOTHING (JUST (5%)) EQUALS JUST 0.5
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 10 120 100 NOTHING (JUST (5%)) EQUALS JUST 0.5
-- S at least F and no order (only the full rate is increased): no paragraph gives an increase.
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 10 100 100 (JUST (10%)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- R plus S at most F (and S below F): paragraphs (3) and (4): the full-rate percentage of R.
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 10 50 100 (JUST (10%)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 1
-- R plus S exactly F: still (3) ("equal to or less than").
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 50 50 100 (JUST (10%)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 5
-- An order alone does nothing in that situation.
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 10 50 100 NOTHING (JUST (5%)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 50 50 100 NOTHING (JUST (5%)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Both events: only the full-rate increase has a paragraph ((3) and (4)); the order has none (finding).
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 10 50 100 (JUST (10%)) (JUST (5%)) EQUALS JUST 1
-- R plus S above F, S below F: paragraphs (5) to (7). R = 60, S = 50, F = 100: shortfall F - S = 50; excess R + S - F = 10.
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 60 50 100 (JUST (10%)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 60 50 100 NOTHING (JUST (5%)) EQUALS JUST 0.5
-- "Either or both": both add together, 5 + 0.5.
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 60 50 100 (JUST (10%)) (JUST (5%)) EQUALS JUST 5.5
-- Neither event: nothing to apply.
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 60 50 100 NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- One pound over F: an order alone gives 5% of the excess, 1 pound: 0.05.
#ASSERT `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` 51 50 100 NOTHING (JUST (5%)) EQUALS JUST 0.05

§ `Fixtures for regulation 18`
`deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice` MEANS DeferredGrbFacts WITH
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death` IS TRUE
    `it was deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS TRUE
    `the person is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
`not deferred at death` MEANS DeferredGrbFacts WITH
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death` IS FALSE
    `it was deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS TRUE
    `the person is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
`deferred at death but not throughout the 12 months` MEANS DeferredGrbFacts WITH
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death` IS TRUE
    `it was deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
`deferred, with a section 8(2) choice` MEANS DeferredGrbFacts WITH
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death` IS TRUE
    `it was deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS TRUE
    `the person is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS TRUE

§ `Regulation 18: entitlement to a choice`

-- (1): reached pensionable age, spouse died while married, GRB deferred at death and
-- throughout the 12 months, and under pensionable age at death without marrying again.
#ASSERT `regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` `person has not yet reached pensionable age on the day` `deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` `the spouse had not died while married` `deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `not deferred at death`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `deferred at death but not throughout the 12 months`)
-- (d)(i) needs no new marriage; (d)(ii) does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` `spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person married again before pensionable age` `deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice`)
#ASSERT `regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person over pensionable age and married again (irrelevant)` `deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` `spouse died on the day the person reaches pensionable age` `deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice`)

-- (8): not entitled to a choice under this regulation if entitled to one under section 8(2).
#ASSERT `regulation 18(1) and (8): the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(1) and (8): the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `deferred, with a section 8(2) choice`)
#ASSERT `regulation 18(8): paragraph (1) applies but the person has a section 8(2) choice instead` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `deferred, with a section 8(2) choice`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(8): paragraph (1) applies but the person has a section 8(2) choice instead` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice`)

-- The date on which the person becomes entitled to make the choice (fork F22): the later of
-- the date they reach pensionable age and the date of the death.
#ASSERT `regulation 18(1): the date on which the person becomes entitled to make the choice` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` EQUALS YMD 2020 1 1
#ASSERT `regulation 18(1): the date on which the person becomes entitled to make the choice` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reached pensionable age 1 May 2016` EQUALS YMD 2016 6 1
#ASSERT `regulation 19(2): the date read in place of the date of becoming entitled to a retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person reached pensionable age 1 May 2016` EQUALS YMD 2016 6 1

§ `Regulation 18(4) to (7): period, late choice, lump sum, alteration`

-- (4): the period is the one in regulation 4(2) and (3).
#ASSERT `regulation 18(4): whether the choice is made within the period` (JUST (YMD 2027 1 15)) (YMD 2027 3 1) `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` (YMD 2027 4 14) EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
#ASSERT `regulation 18(4): whether the choice is made within the period` (JUST (YMD 2027 1 15)) (YMD 2027 3 1) `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` (YMD 2027 4 15) EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`
-- No notice: the period starts on the later of the claim (1 Mar 2027) and the death (1 Mar 2010).
#ASSERT `regulation 18(4): whether the choice is made within the period` NOTHING (YMD 2027 3 1) `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
#ASSERT `regulation 18(4): whether the choice is made within the period` NOTHING (YMD 2027 3 1) `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` (YMD 2027 2 28) EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`

`a late choice that may be made` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS TRUE
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS TRUE

`a late choice that may not be made` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS FALSE
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS FALSE
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS FALSE

-- (4)(a), (b): a late choice on the same conditions as regulation 4(4).
#ASSERT `regulation 18(4): a late choice may be made` `a late choice that may be made`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(4): a late choice may be made` `a late choice that may not be made`)
-- (6): the lump sum under regulation 19 falls to nil on a late choice of a state pension.
#ASSERT `regulation 18(6): the amount of the lump sum` 3500 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `regulation 18(6): the amount of the lump sum` 3500 FALSE EQUALS 3500

`an alteration that meets regulation 6(2)` MEANS AlterationFacts WITH
    `the person who made the choice has since died` IS FALSE
    `an application is made to alter the choice` IS TRUE
    `the date of the application` IS YMD 2027 3 1
    `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice` IS YMD 2027 1 15
    `the last day of any longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS NOTHING
    `the manner of the application` IS `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State`
    `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS FALSE
    `the choice the application asks for` IS `a state pension`
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS FALSE
    `the date on which the repayment in full was completed` IS YMD 2027 2 20
    `that amount was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS FALSE
    `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` IS 10000
    `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS 12000
    `a previous alteration has been made in respect of the same deferral` IS FALSE
    `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 1987` IS FALSE

`an alteration made too late` MEANS AlterationFacts WITH
    `the person who made the choice has since died` IS FALSE
    `an application is made to alter the choice` IS TRUE
    `the date of the application` IS YMD 2027 9 1
    `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice` IS YMD 2027 1 15
    `the last day of any longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS NOTHING
    `the manner of the application` IS `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State`
    `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS FALSE
    `the choice the application asks for` IS `a state pension`
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS FALSE
    `the date on which the repayment in full was completed` IS YMD 2027 2 20
    `that amount was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS FALSE
    `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` IS 10000
    `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS 12000
    `a previous alteration has been made in respect of the same deferral` IS FALSE
    `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 1987` IS FALSE

-- (7): an alteration under regulation 6(2) applies to this choice as it does to a choice under section 8(2).
#ASSERT `regulation 18(7): the choice may be altered` `an alteration that meets regulation 6(2)`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 18(7): the choice may be altered` `an alteration made too late`)

§ `Regulation 18(2), (5), (9) to (11): what the person is to be paid`

`chose a lump sum in time` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS JUST `a lump sum`
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS FALSE

`chose a state pension in time` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS JUST `a state pension`
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS FALSE

`made no choice` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS FALSE
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS FALSE

`chose a state pension too late` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS JUST `a state pension`
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS FALSE
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS FALSE

`chose a lump sum, then altered to a state pension` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS JUST `a lump sum`
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS JUST `a state pension`
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS TRUE

`chose a state pension, asked to alter to a lump sum, alteration refused` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS JUST `a state pension`
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS JUST `a lump sum`
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS FALSE

`chose a state pension, then altered to a lump sum` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS JUST `a state pension`
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS JUST `a lump sum`
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS TRUE

`outside paragraph (1)` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS FALSE
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS JUST `a state pension`
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS TRUE
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `chose a lump sum in time` EQUALS `a lump sum under regulation 19`
#ASSERT `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `chose a state pension in time` EQUALS `a state pension under regulation 20`
-- (5), (11): no choice (or none in time): a lump sum.
#ASSERT `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `made no choice` EQUALS `a lump sum under regulation 19`
#ASSERT `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `chose a state pension too late` EQUALS `a lump sum under regulation 19`
-- (7), (10): an allowed alteration replaces the choice.
#ASSERT `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `chose a lump sum, then altered to a state pension` EQUALS `a state pension under regulation 20`
#ASSERT `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `chose a state pension, then altered to a lump sum` EQUALS `a lump sum under regulation 19`
-- A refused alteration leaves the original choice.
#ASSERT `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `chose a state pension, asked to alter to a lump sum, alteration refused` EQUALS `a state pension under regulation 20`
-- Outside paragraph (1): not covered.
#ASSERT `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `outside paragraph (1)` EQUALS `regulation 18 does not cover the person`

§ `Regulation 19: the lump sum`

#ASSERT `regulation 19(1): the lump sum payable` `a lump sum under regulation 19` 3500 EQUALS JUST 3500
#ASSERT `regulation 19(1): the lump sum payable` `a state pension under regulation 20` 3500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `regulation 19(1): the lump sum payable` `regulation 18 does not cover the person` 3500 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Fixtures for regulation 20`
`the spouse was entitled to an increase` MEANS IncreaseFacts WITH
    `the spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS TRUE
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died` IS FALSE
`the spouse was entitled to no increase and nothing was deferred` MEANS IncreaseFacts WITH
    `the spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died` IS FALSE
`the spouse had deferred, with no increase yet` MEANS IncreaseFacts WITH
    `the spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died` IS TRUE

§ `Regulation 20: entitlement to the survivor's state pension`

-- (a) to (d), with no regulation 18 choice in play (the outcome is "not covered", so (e) and (f) are vacuous).
#ASSERT `regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `the spouse was entitled to an increase` `regulation 18 does not cover the person`
-- (e), (f): where regulation 18 applies, the outcome must be a state pension.
#ASSERT `regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `the spouse had deferred, with no increase yet` `a state pension under regulation 20`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `the spouse had deferred, with no increase yet` `a lump sum under regulation 19`)
-- (a): reached pensionable age.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `person has not yet reached pensionable age on the day` `the spouse was entitled to an increase` `regulation 18 does not cover the person`)
-- (b): died while married.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `the spouse had not died while married` `the spouse was entitled to an increase` `regulation 18 does not cover the person`)
-- (c): under pensionable age without a new marriage, or over pensionable age; neither if exactly at it.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person married again before pensionable age` `the spouse was entitled to an increase` `regulation 18 does not cover the person`)
#ASSERT `regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `spouse died 1 Jun 2016, person over pensionable age and married again (irrelevant)` `the spouse was entitled to an increase` `regulation 18 does not cover the person`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `spouse died on the day the person reaches pensionable age` `the spouse was entitled to an increase` `regulation 18 does not cover the person`)
-- (d): an increase, or a deferral at death; neither fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `base: spouse died 1 Mar 2010, person reaches pensionable age 1 Jan 2020` `the spouse was entitled to no increase and nothing was deferred` `regulation 18 does not cover the person`)

-- (2): half of the increase; (3): up-rated by the order's percentage.
#ASSERT `regulation 20(2): the weekly rate of the state pension under regulation 20` 12 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `regulation 20(2): the weekly rate of the state pension under regulation 20` 12.50 EQUALS 6.25
#ASSERT `regulation 20(3): the rate after an order under section 151A of the Administration Act` 6 (5%) EQUALS 6.3
#ASSERT `regulation 20(3): the rate after an order under section 151A of the Administration Act` 6 (0%) EQUALS 6
